# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rust / Cargo
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Build output. 100% regenerable by `cargo build`; often hundreds of MB.
# This is the single most important line in the file.
target/

# Old rustfmt backups.
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC debug symbols (only produced by the windows-msvc target).
*.pdb

# NOTE: Cargo.lock is deliberately NOT ignored.
#   - application / binary crate  -> COMMIT it (reproducible builds)
#   - reusable library crate      -> historically ignored, now usually committed too
# Every crate here is a binary, so committing it is correct.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Profiling & coverage (you will hit these in Phase 9)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.profraw
*.profdata
perf.data
perf.data.old
flamegraph.svg
cargo-timing*.html

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors / IDEs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/*
# ...but keep shared project config if you ever add it:
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/tasks.json

# Vim / Emacs / temp files
*~
*.swp
*.swo
\#*\#
.\#*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS junk
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Windows
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
# macOS / Linux
.DS_Store
.directory

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local environment — never push these
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.local
*.local
.direnv/
